@startuml fig5_overview
' Diagram 5 of the VDI 3682 pattern: the whole of it.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md, section 8. This diagram is for the
' documentation rather than for a paper, and it therefore shows every class of
' the pattern. Diagrams 1 to 4 are the readable cuts through it.
'
' What it shows: all fifteen classes and the relations between them, grouped by
' the three questions the pattern answers: what the process is, what passes
' through it, and what performs it.
'
' Left out on purpose: the data properties of the two attribute classes, which
' diagram 4 carries, and the general hasSource and hasTarget of the flow, which
' say nothing the four specific relations do not.
'
' Of each inverse pair only one direction is drawn, as in diagram 1. The
' ontology declares hasUpperProcess alongside hasSubProcess and hasPredecessor
' alongside hasSuccessor.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 42
skinparam padding 2
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 12
  BorderThickness 1
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #8A98A8
  BackgroundColor #FCFDFE
  FontColor #33475B
  FontSize 12
  FontStyle italic
}

package "What the process is" {
  class Process
  class ProcessOperator
  class SystemLimit
}

package "What passes through it" {
  class State
  class Product
  class Energy
  class Information
  class Flow
  class ParallelFlow
  class AlternativeFlow
}

package "What performs it" {
  class Assignment
  class TechnicalResource
  class Attribute
  class Identification
  class Characteristic
}

State <|-- Product
State <|-- Energy
State <|-- Information
Flow  <|-- ParallelFlow
Flow  <|-- AlternativeFlow
Attribute <|-- Identification
Attribute <|-- Characteristic

Process         --> ProcessOperator : consistsOf
ProcessOperator --> Process         : hasSubProcess
ProcessOperator --> ProcessOperator : isComposedOf
ProcessOperator --> ProcessOperator : hasSuccessor
ProcessOperator --> SystemLimit     : isWithin

ProcessOperator --> State : hasInput
ProcessOperator --> State : hasOutput
State           --> State : dependency

Flow --> State           : hasStateSource
Flow --> ProcessOperator : hasOperatorTarget
Flow --> ProcessOperator : hasOperatorSource
Flow --> State           : hasStateTarget

ProcessOperator   --> Assignment        : hasAssignment
Assignment        --> TechnicalResource : assignedResource
ProcessOperator   --> TechnicalResource : isAssignedTo
TechnicalResource --> Identification    : isIdentifiedBy
TechnicalResource --> Characteristic    : isCharacterizedBy

@enduml
